# Homepage-anchor routes — folded into the homepage in the redesign (App.tsx
# uses <Navigate> to the matching #anchor). Server-side 301 so Google and other
# crawlers consolidate them into the homepage instead of crawling empty SPA
# shells (previously these showed as "Discovered – currently not indexed").
# Both the no-slash and trailing-slash forms are covered.
#
# The target is the bare homepage, with no #fragment. A fragment is never sent
# to the server, so a crawler resolves "/pricing -> /#pricing" as a redirect to
# "/" anyway; spelling it out keeps the redirect target unambiguous in Search
# Console and avoids a target that looks like it differs from the canonical
# homepage when it does not.
/how-it-works    /   301
/how-it-works/   /   301
/pricing         /   301
/pricing/        /   301
/portfolio       /   301
/portfolio/      /   301
/faq             /   301
/faq/            /   301
/contact         /   301
/contact/        /   301

# Retired redesign-preview path
/new/*           /   301
